/-! ## The walk step

Write `w(x) = ⌊x √3⌋`.  From one element `m` of the intersection to the next one `m + g`, the
quantity `w(m + g + 1) - w(m + 1)` is determined by the gap alone: `4` across a gap of `2`, `5` across a gap of `3`, `9` across a gap of `5`, `10` across a gap of `6`.
This is the step rule behind the drift of the sequence (see `beatty-intersections/drift-proof.md`). -/

theorem core_walk {t s : ℝ} (hslo : 1.732 < s) (hshi : s < 1.7321) (m k l : ℤ)
    (h1 : t ≤ 3 * (k : ℝ)) (h2 : 3 * (k : ℝ) < t + s)
    (h3 : t - (m : ℝ) ≤ 2 * (l : ℝ)) (h4 : 2 * (l : ℝ) < t - (m : ℝ) + (s - 1)) :
